{"id":"XqAMiQ7K4JIwuALa","meta":{"instanceId":"93f396852104089b8670e7494b0f3668b420464668ae4a8c1d6b4b5799f8e3ef","templateCredsSetupCompleted":true},"name":"Pool Service Visit Generator","tags":[],"nodes":[{"id":"74153a7b-88da-4941-b370-404885818579","name":"Sticky Note","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[4096,2112],"parameters":{"width":480,"height":864,"content":"## Pool Service Visit Generator\n\n### How it works\n\n1. Receives technician visit details via a form trigger and verifies customer records against Google Sheets.\\n2. Formulates historical context and utilizes Gemini AI to structure service visit notes and identify follow-up actions.\\n3. Logs visit logs and updates customer data, generating work orders and Slack alerts if follow-ups or urgent matters arise.\\n4. Manages an approval cycle for report delivery, emailing the finalized service report to the customer upon confirmation.\\n5. Runs a scheduled daily routine to compile open work orders into a Telegram digest and triggers Telegram alerts on errors.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- - [ ] Configure Google Sheets credentials and link the spreadsheets for customers, visit history, and work orders.\n- - [ ] Connect Google Gemini API credentials in the Notes Structuring Agent node.\n- - [ ] Set up Gmail credentials for sending customer reports and manager approval requests.\n- - [ ] Configure Slack and Telegram integrations for operational alerts and daily digests.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the chemical and inspection thresholds in the Prep Context node, and customize email templates or Slack notification channels to match internal team structure.\n\n@[youtube](uAWvXz7FrzI)"},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"fd31503d-d4ff-4118-89ec-fa62905fae1e","name":"Sticky Note1","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[4640,2096],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":640,"height":304,"content":"## Verify customer from form\n\nCaptures technician visit form submission and validates customer presence in Google Sheets."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"e9ebd87a-dd3c-413f-83a4-06041cedf573","name":"Sticky Note2","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[5312,2128],"parameters":{"color":7,"height":352,"content":"## Notify missing customer record\n\nSends a Telegram alert if the customer specified on the form is not found."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"c58cba99-c493-4197-b6c8-0fc6e2126002","name":"Sticky Note3","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[5312,1792],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":416,"height":304,"content":"## Retrieve customer visit history\n\nPulls previous visit history and prepares context and thresholds for AI evaluation."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"ad0d4a20-505c-4ef8-aaea-7a3c789f4b6d","name":"Sticky Note4","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[5744,1792],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":352,"height":512,"content":"## Structure notes with AI\n\nUses Gemini LLM to parse and structure technician notes into organized data."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"6e0e3203-1df2-4273-a93b-b38da0f9dece","name":"Sticky Note5","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[6128,1888],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":640,"height":304,"content":"## Handle AI processing failure\n\nCaptures AI parsing failures, logs them into Google Sheets, and notifies the team via Slack."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"15d62218-2fd1-46f1-a9e7-10a5a85335fb","name":"Sticky Note6","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[6128,1552],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":416,"height":304,"content":"## Record completed visit\n\nBuilds a structured visit payload and records the visit in Google Sheets."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"90b65c1a-ee21-43cf-86c9-9c36eafd48bb","name":"Sticky Note7","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[6576,1472],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":640,"height":384,"content":"## Manage follow-ups and work orders\n\nEvaluates if follow-up is needed, creates work orders, and updates customer status in sheets."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"58b909c3-d612-47bb-aaae-f083e5e75f55","name":"Sticky Note8","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[7248,1616],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":416,"height":384,"content":"## Alert urgent service issues\n\nChecks if urgent action is required and posts instant notifications to Slack."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"41812804-3376-4b9a-8c16-1d10ad0477b3","name":"Sticky Note9","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[7696,1584],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":1088,"height":400,"content":"## Manage manager report approvals\n\nSends manager approval emails, pauses workflow for approval response, and handles held reports."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"cb7eed33-cafa-4882-9509-8fa76cabfaf3","name":"Sticky Note10","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[8608,2000],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":416,"height":304,"content":"## Send visit report to customer\n\nEmails the final service visit summary to the customer and marks the visit report as sent."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"87c8c605-75a0-4d24-8d91-42bec13c63ce","name":"Sticky Note11","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[4640,2512],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":864,"height":272,"content":"## Daily open work orders digest\n\nRuns daily at 7:30 AM to collect open work orders and dispatch a digest via Telegram."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"ad281fe8-6f71-450f-b6f0-82c7cbf6ebc7","name":"Sticky Note12","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[4640,2816],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":416,"height":304,"content":"## Workflow error alerting\n\nCatches unexpected workflow errors and dispatches alert messages to Telegram."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"662a41f1-f6d2-4906-bc6d-e6694324978d","name":"When Technician Submits Form","type":"n8n-nodes-base.formTrigger","position":[4688,2224],"webhookId":"343134b1-28aa-407f-851e-720518bcdeb3","parameters":{"options":{},"formTitle":"Pool Service Visit","formFields":{"values":[{"fieldLabel":"Customer ID","placeholder":"C-1001","requiredField":true},{"fieldLabel":"Technician Name","requiredField":true},{"fieldType":"date","fieldLabel":"Visit Date","requiredField":true},{"fieldType":"number","fieldLabel":"Free Chlorine (ppm)","placeholder":"optional"},{"fieldType":"number","fieldLabel":"pH","placeholder":"optional"},{"fieldType":"number","fieldLabel":"Total Alkalinity (ppm)","placeholder":"optional"},{"fieldType":"number","fieldLabel":"Filter Pressure (psi)","placeholder":"optional"},{"fieldType":"textarea","fieldLabel":"Technician Notes","placeholder":"Pool looked cloudy, chlorine low, filter pressure high...","requiredField":true}]},"formDescription":"Log your visit. Messy notes are fine."},"typeVersion":2.2},{"id":"b3e7f205-397d-403e-9229-1d7ccb8e97f0","name":"Fetch Customer Details","type":"n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets","position":[4912,2224],"parameters":{"options":{"returnFirstMatch":true},"filtersUI":{"values":[{"lookupValue":"={{ $('When Technician Submits Form').first().json['Customer ID'].trim() }}","lookupColumn":"Customer ID"}]},"sheetName":{"__rl":true,"mode":"name","value":"Customers"},"documentId":{"__rl":true,"mode":"id","value":"1dx-1KrMuwi8POXiKNTix8induDZPPcycrBCchfx4kDM"},"authentication":"serviceAccount"},"credentials":{"googleApi":{"id":"credential-id","name":"Google Service Account account"}},"typeVersion":4.5,"alwaysOutputData":true},{"id":"5f9dbf7f-8462-4755-bc49-59941d07d19b","name":"If Customer Found","type":"n8n-nodes-base.if","position":[5136,2224],"parameters":{"options":{},"conditions":{"options":{"version":2,"leftValue":"","caseSensitive":true,"typeValidation":"loose"},"combinator":"and","conditions":[{"id":"1be5c24f-fd07-43cd-bedb-cee3377ea463","operator":{"type":"string","operation":"notEmpty","singleValue":true},"leftValue":"={{ $json['Customer ID'] }}"}]}},"typeVersion":2.2},{"id":"eb102b07-6022-464a-94be-b10424e199b7","name":"Send Unknown Customer Alert","type":"n8n-nodes-base.telegram","position":[5360,2320],"webhookId":"883ea491-0bfc-4c58-b1c6-9175959d36ab","parameters":{"text":"={{ '⚠️ Unknown Customer ID \"' + $('When Technician Submits Form').first().json['Customer ID'] + '\" from ' + $('When Technician Submits Form').first().json['Technician Name'] + '. Visit notes were NOT processed:\\n\\n' + $('When Technician Submits Form').first().json['Technician Notes'] }}","chatId":"YOUR_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID","additionalFields":{"appendAttribution":false}},"credentials":{"telegramApi":{"id":"credential-id","name":"Telegram account 6"}},"typeVersion":1.2},{"id":"7892cb5d-2cab-449f-8469-9b0c1343408e","name":"Fetch Visit History","type":"n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets","position":[5360,1920],"parameters":{"options":{},"filtersUI":{"values":[{"lookupValue":"={{ $('Fetch Customer Details').first().json['Customer ID'] }}","lookupColumn":"Customer ID"}]},"sheetName":{"__rl":true,"mode":"name","value":"Visits"},"documentId":{"__rl":true,"mode":"id","value":"1dx-1KrMuwi8POXiKNTix8induDZPPcycrBCchfx4kDM"},"authentication":"serviceAccount"},"credentials":{"googleApi":{"id":"credential-id","name":"Google Service Account account"}},"typeVersion":4.5,"alwaysOutputData":true},{"id":"35cac259-af24-4368-b950-63cf55a8dea4","name":"Prepare Agent Context","type":"n8n-nodes-base.code","position":[5584,1920],"parameters":{"jsCode":"// ===== CONFIG (edit thresholds here) =====\nconst CFG = {\n  RANGES: {\n    free_chlorine: { label: 'Free chlorine',    unit: 'ppm', min: 1,   max: 5,   severeLow: 0.5, severeHigh: 8 },\n    ph:            { label: 'pH',                unit: '',    min: 7.2, max: 7.8, severeLow: 6.8, severeHigh: 8.2 },\n    alkalinity:    { label: 'Total alkalinity', unit: 'ppm', min: 80,  max: 120, severeLow: 50,  severeHigh: 180 }\n  },\n  PSI_OVER_BASELINE: 8,   // flag filter if this many psi above the customer's clean baseline\n  PSI_ABS_LIMIT: 30       // used when no baseline is on file\n};\n// =========================================\nconst form = $('When Technician Submits Form').first().json;\nconst cust = $('Fetch Customer Details').first().json;\nconst hist = $input.all().map(i => i.json).filter(r => r['Visit ID'])\n  .sort((a, b) => String(b['Visit Date']).localeCompare(String(a['Visit Date'])))\n  .slice(0, 3);\n\nconst num = v => (v === '' || v === null || v === undefined || isNaN(Number(v))) ? null : Number(v);\nconst readings = {\n  free_chlorine: num(form['Free Chlorine (ppm)']),\n  ph: num(form['pH']),\n  alkalinity: num(form['Total Alkalinity (ppm)']),\n  filter_psi: num(form['Filter Pressure (psi)'])\n};\nconst paramName = { free_chlorine: 'Chlorine', ph: 'pH', alkalinity: 'Alkalinity' };\nconst flags = [];\nconst table = [];\n\nfor (const [key, r] of Object.entries(CFG.RANGES)) {\n  const v = readings[key];\n  if (v === null) continue;\n  let status = 'OK';\n  if (v < r.min) status = 'Low'; else if (v > r.max) status = 'High';\n  const u = r.unit ? ' ' + r.unit : '';\n  table.push({ label: r.label, value: `${v}${u}`, target: `${r.min}-${r.max}${u}`, status });\n  if (status !== 'OK') {\n    const severe = v <= r.severeLow || v >= r.severeHigh;\n    flags.push({ type: 'chemical', parameter: paramName[key], issue: `${status} (${v}${u})`, severity: severe ? 'Severe' : 'Moderate' });\n  }\n}\n\nconst baseline = num(cust['Baseline Filter PSI']);\nif (readings.filter_psi !== null) {\n  const limit = baseline !== null ? baseline + CFG.PSI_OVER_BASELINE : CFG.PSI_ABS_LIMIT;\n  const high = readings.filter_psi >= limit;\n  table.push({ label: 'Filter pressure', value: `${readings.filter_psi} psi`, target: `below ${limit} psi`, status: high ? 'High' : 'OK' });\n  if (high) flags.push({ type: 'equipment', equipment: 'Filter',\n    issue: `High pressure (${readings.filter_psi} psi` + (baseline !== null ? `, clean baseline ${baseline}` : '') + ')',\n    severity: 'Moderate', suggested_action: 'Clean' });\n}\n\nconst flagText = flags.length ? flags.map(f => `- ${f.parameter || f.equipment}: ${f.issue} [${f.severity}]`).join('\\n') : '- none';\nconst readingsText = table.length ? table.map(t => `${t.label} ${t.value} (${t.status})`).join(', ') : 'none provided';\nconst historyText = hist.length\n  ? hist.map(h => `- ${h['Visit Date']}: ${h['Pool Condition']} | Chem: ${h['Chemical Issues']} | Equip: ${h['Equipment Issues']}`).join('\\n')\n  : '- no previous visits on file';\n\nconst agent_input = `CUSTOMER: ${cust['Customer Name']} | pool: ${cust['Pool Type'] || 'unknown'}, ${cust['Volume (gal)'] || '?'} gal | plan: ${cust['Service Plan'] || 'Weekly'}\nVISIT DATE: ${form['Visit Date']}\nREADINGS PROVIDED: ${readingsText}\nRULE-BASED FLAGS (verified from readings, include them):\n${flagText}\nRECENT VISITS (newest first):\n${historyText}\nTECHNICIAN NOTES (raw):\n\"\"\"\n${form['Technician Notes']}\n\"\"\"`;\n\nreturn [{ json: {\n  customer_id: cust['Customer ID'],\n  customer_name: cust['Customer Name'],\n  customer_email: cust['Email'] || '',\n  property_address: cust['Address'] || '',\n  service_plan: cust['Service Plan'] || 'Weekly',\n  assigned_tech: cust['Assigned Tech'] || '',\n  technician: form['Technician Name'],\n  visit_date: form['Visit Date'] || $now.toFormat('yyyy-LL-dd'),\n  raw_notes: form['Technician Notes'],\n  readings, readings_table: table, readings_text: readingsText === 'none provided' ? '' : readingsText,\n  rule_flags: flags, history: hist, agent_input\n} }];"},"typeVersion":2},{"id":"98fdb125-7062-497f-a399-39344ae3ee3f","name":"Structure Notes Agent","type":"@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent","onError":"continueErrorOutput","maxTries":2,"position":[5792,1920],"parameters":{"text":"={{ $json.agent_input }}","options":{"systemMessage":"You turn messy pool-technician field notes into structured operational data for a pool maintenance company. You are doing data entry and triage, NOT giving medical, legal, or safety rulings.\n\nRULES\n1. Extract only what the notes, readings, or rule-based flags support. Never invent readings, chemicals, equipment, or actions.\n2. Rule-based flags come from the technician's measured readings and are verified. Always include them in your issues (you may add detail from the notes).\n3. If notes and readings conflict, trust the readings and mention the conflict in missing_info.\n4. Anything vague or absent (no readings, \"the thing by the pump\", unclear what was done) goes in missing_info. Do not guess.\n5. Use RECENT VISITS only to spot patterns (repeat issues). Mention a repeat in internal_notes. Do not copy old issues into today's list unless today's notes confirm them.\n6. pool_condition: Good = no issues. Needs attention = one or more issues to correct. Critical = unswimmable/green water, no circulation, equipment failure, leak, or a hazard.\n7. water_clarity: Clear, Slightly cloudy, Cloudy, Green, or Unknown.\n8. chemical_issues: one entry per problem. parameter e.g. Chlorine, pH, Alkalinity, Stabilizer, Salt, Calcium, Algae, Clarity. issue is short (\"Low\", \"High\", \"Algae starting\"). severity: Minor, Moderate, or Severe.\n9. equipment_issues: one entry per problem. equipment e.g. Filter, Pump, Heater, Skimmer, Salt cell, Cleaner, Timer, Cover. suggested_action: Monitor, Clean, Repair, Replace, or Inspect. quote_needed = true only if repair/replacement work beyond routine service is implied.\n10. actions_taken: only what the technician says they did.\n11. safety_concerns: physical hazards the technician explicitly mentions (broken drain cover, loose ladder, gate latch, electrical). Otherwise an empty array.\n12. swim_advisory: ONLY if the technician explicitly says to avoid swimming or restrict use. Quote their intent in plain words. Otherwise an empty string. Never decide this yourself.\n13. recommended_follow_up: true if anything remains unresolved or needs a re-check or separate trip.\n14. follow_up_type: None, Re-test water, Chemical correction visit, Equipment repair, Filter service, Inspection, or Quote required.\n15. next_visit_days: use the technician's own timing if stated. Otherwise Good = the customer's normal plan interval, Needs attention = 3 (up to 5 if minor), Critical = 1 or 2.\n16. urgency: Routine, Soon, or Urgent.\n17. customer_summary: 2-3 friendly plain sentences for the homeowner. No jargon, no blame, no prices, no promises about swimming safety.\n18. confidence: High, Medium, or Low, based on how complete and clear the notes were.\n19. internal_notes: one or two lines for the office team (patterns, upsell or parts hints). Never shown to the customer."},"promptType":"define","hasOutputParser":true},"retryOnFail":true,"typeVersion":1.7,"waitBetweenTries":2000},{"id":"dc7e832c-fb52-4fbb-8466-1527e608cbde","name":"Google Gemini Model","type":"@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatGoogleGemini","position":[5808,2144],"parameters":{"options":{"temperature":0.1},"modelName":"models/gemini-3.1-flash-lite"},"credentials":{"googlePalmApi":{"id":"credential-id","name":"STRICTLY USE GEMINI-3.1-FLASH-LITE"}},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"c3d678be-e37b-4535-b1ff-caf98593d56d","name":"Parse Structured Output","type":"@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.outputParserStructured","position":[5936,2144],"parameters":{"schemaType":"manual","inputSchema":"{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"pool_condition\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"Good\",\n        \"Needs attention\",\n        \"Critical\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"water_clarity\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"Clear\",\n        \"Slightly cloudy\",\n        \"Cloudy\",\n        \"Green\",\n        \"Unknown\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"chemical_issues\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"parameter\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"issue\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"severity\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"enum\": [\n              \"Minor\",\n              \"Moderate\",\n              \"Severe\"\n            ]\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"parameter\",\n          \"issue\",\n          \"severity\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    \"equipment_issues\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"equipment\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"issue\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"severity\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"enum\": [\n              \"Minor\",\n              \"Moderate\",\n              \"Severe\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"suggested_action\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"enum\": [\n              \"Monitor\",\n              \"Clean\",\n              \"Repair\",\n              \"Replace\",\n              \"Inspect\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"quote_needed\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"equipment\",\n          \"issue\",\n          \"severity\",\n          \"suggested_action\",\n          \"quote_needed\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    \"actions_taken\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"safety_concerns\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"swim_advisory\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"recommended_follow_up\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"follow_up_type\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"None\",\n        \"Re-test water\",\n        \"Chemical correction visit\",\n        \"Equipment repair\",\n        \"Filter service\",\n        \"Inspection\",\n        \"Quote required\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"next_visit_days\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"urgency\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"Routine\",\n        \"Soon\",\n        \"Urgent\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"customer_summary\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"High\",\n        \"Medium\",\n        \"Low\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"missing_info\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"internal_notes\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"pool_condition\",\n    \"water_clarity\",\n    \"chemical_issues\",\n    \"equipment_issues\",\n    \"actions_taken\",\n    \"safety_concerns\",\n    \"swim_advisory\",\n    \"recommended_follow_up\",\n    \"follow_up_type\",\n    \"next_visit_days\",\n    \"urgency\",\n    \"customer_summary\",\n    \"confidence\",\n    \"missing_info\",\n    \"internal_notes\"\n  ]\n}"},"typeVersion":1.2},{"id":"df96fcbf-45da-469c-af76-813bd81dc8e1","name":"Build Visit Record","type":"n8n-nodes-base.code","position":[6176,1680],"parameters":{"jsCode":"// ===== CONFIG (edit me) =====\nconst C = {\n  COMPANY: 'Your Pool Company',\n  PHONE: '+1234567890',\n  BRAND: '#0e7490',\n  SKIP_SUNDAY: true,\n  MAX_DAYS: 30,\n  PLAN_DAYS: { weekly: 7, biweekly: 14, 'bi-weekly': 14, monthly: 30 }\n};\n// =============================\nconst ctx = $('Prepare Agent Context').first().json;\nconst ai = $input.first().json.output || {};\n\nconst esc = s => String(s ?? '').replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;');\nconst arr = v => Array.isArray(v) ? v : [];\nconst lc = s => String(s ?? '').toLowerCase();\nconst pick = (v, list, d) => list.includes(v) ? v : d;\nconst SEV = ['Minor', 'Moderate', 'Severe'];\nconst sevRank = s => Math.max(0, SEV.indexOf(s));\nconst rid = () => Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 6).toUpperCase();\n\n// ---------- 1. clean AI output ----------\nconst chem = arr(ai.chemical_issues).filter(c => c && c.parameter).map(c => ({\n  parameter: String(c.parameter), issue: String(c.issue || ''), severity: pick(c.severity, SEV, 'Moderate') }));\nconst equip = arr(ai.equipment_issues).filter(e => e && e.equipment).map(e => ({\n  equipment: String(e.equipment), issue: String(e.issue || ''), severity: pick(e.severity, SEV, 'Moderate'),\n  suggested_action: pick(e.suggested_action, ['Monitor', 'Clean', 'Repair', 'Replace', 'Inspect'], 'Inspect'),\n  quote_needed: e.quote_needed === true }));\n\n// ---------- 2. rules win: merge measured-reading flags ----------\nfor (const f of arr(ctx.rule_flags)) {\n  if (f.type === 'chemical') {\n    const hit = chem.find(c => lc(c.parameter).includes(lc(f.parameter)) || lc(f.parameter).includes(lc(c.parameter)));\n    if (hit) { if (sevRank(f.severity) > sevRank(hit.severity)) hit.severity = f.severity; hit.issue = f.issue; }\n    else chem.push({ parameter: f.parameter, issue: f.issue, severity: f.severity });\n  } else {\n    const hit = equip.find(e => lc(e.equipment).includes(lc(f.equipment)) || lc(f.equipment).includes(lc(e.equipment)));\n    if (hit) { if (sevRank(f.severity) > sevRank(hit.severity)) hit.severity = f.severity; hit.issue = f.issue; }\n    else equip.push({ equipment: f.equipment, issue: f.issue, severity: f.severity, suggested_action: f.suggested_action || 'Inspect', quote_needed: false });\n  }\n}\n\n// ---------- 3. recurrence vs last 3 visits ----------\nconst hist = arr(ctx.history);\nconst prior = (field, name) => hist.filter(h => lc(h[field]).includes(lc(name))).length;\nconst recurring = [];\nfor (const c of chem) { const n = prior('Chemical Issues', c.parameter); if (n >= 2) recurring.push(`${c.parameter} (in ${n} of last ${hist.length} visits)`); }\nfor (const e of equip) { const n = prior('Equipment Issues', e.equipment); if (n >= 2) recurring.push(`${e.equipment} (in ${n} of last ${hist.length} visits)`); }\n\n// ---------- 4. condition / urgency / follow-up ----------\nconst safety = arr(ai.safety_concerns).map(String).filter(Boolean);\nconst hasIssues = chem.length + equip.length > 0;\nconst anySevere = [...chem, ...equip].some(i => i.severity === 'Severe');\nconst clarity = pick(ai.water_clarity, ['Clear', 'Slightly cloudy', 'Cloudy', 'Green', 'Unknown'], 'Unknown');\n\nlet condition = pick(ai.pool_condition, ['Good', 'Needs attention', 'Critical'], 'Needs attention');\nif (hasIssues && condition === 'Good') condition = 'Needs attention';\nif (safety.length || clarity === 'Green') condition = 'Critical';\n\nlet urgency = pick(ai.urgency, ['Routine', 'Soon', 'Urgent'], 'Routine');\nif (condition === 'Critical') urgency = 'Urgent';\nelse if ((hasIssues || anySevere || recurring.length) && urgency === 'Routine') urgency = 'Soon';\n\nconst followUp = ai.recommended_follow_up === true || condition === 'Critical' || recurring.length > 0 || anySevere || equip.length > 0;\nlet ftype = pick(ai.follow_up_type, ['None', 'Re-test water', 'Chemical correction visit', 'Equipment repair', 'Filter service', 'Inspection', 'Quote required'], 'None');\nif (followUp && ftype === 'None') ftype = equip.length ? 'Equipment repair' : 'Re-test water';\nif (recurring.length) ftype = 'Inspection';\nif (!followUp) ftype = 'None';\nconst quoteNeeded = equip.some(e => e.quote_needed) || ftype === 'Quote required';\n\n// ---------- 5. next visit ----------\nconst planDays = C.PLAN_DAYS[lc(ctx.service_plan)] || 7;\nlet days = Math.round(Number(ai.next_visit_days));\nif (!Number.isFinite(days)) days = planDays;\ndays = Math.min(C.MAX_DAYS, Math.max(1, days));\nif (condition === 'Good' && !followUp) days = planDays;\nif (followUp && hasIssues) days = Math.min(days, 5);\nif (recurring.length) days = Math.min(days, 3);\nif (urgency === 'Urgent') days = Math.min(days, 2);\n\nlet visitDate = ctx.visit_date;\nlet d = new Date(visitDate + 'T00:00:00Z');\nif (isNaN(d)) { visitDate = $now.toFormat('yyyy-LL-dd'); d = new Date(visitDate + 'T00:00:00Z'); }\nconst base = new Date(visitDate + 'T00:00:00Z');\nd.setUTCDate(d.getUTCDate() + days);\nif (C.SKIP_SUNDAY && d.getUTCDay() === 0) d.setUTCDate(d.getUTCDate() + 1);\nconst nextDate = d.toISOString().slice(0, 10);\nconst effDays = Math.round((d - base) / 86400000);\n\nconst priority = urgency === 'Urgent' ? 'P1 - Urgent' : (urgency === 'Soon' || recurring.length) ? 'P2 - High' : 'P3 - Normal';\nconst confidence = pick(ai.confidence, ['High', 'Medium', 'Low'], 'Medium');\nconst missing = arr(ai.missing_info).map(String).filter(Boolean);\nconst stamp = visitDate.replace(/-/g, '');\nconst visitId = `PV-${stamp}-${rid()}`;\nconst woId = followUp ? `WO-${stamp}-${rid()}` : '';\n\n// ---------- 6. approval gate ----------\nconst reasons = [];\nif (condition === 'Critical') reasons.push('Critical condition');\nif (safety.length) reasons.push('Safety concern: ' + safety.join(', '));\nif (confidence === 'Low') reasons.push('Low AI confidence');\nif (missing.length && condition !== 'Good') reasons.push('Missing info: ' + missing.join(', '));\nif (lc(ai.pool_condition) === 'good' && arr(ctx.rule_flags).length) reasons.push('AI said Good but readings are out of range');\nif (!ctx.customer_email) reasons.push('No customer email on file');\nconst needsApproval = reasons.length > 0;\n\n// ---------- 7. flat strings ----------\nconst chemText = chem.map(c => `${c.parameter}: ${c.issue}`).join('; ') || 'None noted';\nconst equipText = equip.map(e => `${e.equipment}: ${e.issue}`).join('; ') || 'None noted';\nconst actions = arr(ai.actions_taken).map(String).filter(Boolean);\nconst openIssues = [chemText, equipText].filter(t => t !== 'None noted').join('; ') || 'None';\nconst swim = String(ai.swim_advisory || '').trim();\n\n// ---------- 8. customer report ----------\nconst condColor = { 'Good': '#16a34a', 'Needs attention': '#d97706', 'Critical': '#dc2626' }[condition];\nconst sevColor = { Minor: '#ca8a04', Moderate: '#d97706', Severe: '#dc2626' };\nconst chip = (t, c) => `<span style=\"background:${c};color:#fff;padding:2px 9px;border-radius:10px;font-size:12px;white-space:nowrap\">${esc(t)}</span>`;\nconst td = 'padding:9px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid #eef0f2;font-size:14px;vertical-align:top';\nconst th = 'padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;font-size:12px;color:#6b7280;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em;border-bottom:2px solid #e5e7eb';\n\nconst issueRows = [\n  ...chem.map(c => ({ area: 'Water chemistry', name: c.parameter, detail: c.issue, sev: c.severity })),\n  ...equip.map(e => ({ area: 'Equipment', name: e.equipment, detail: `${e.issue} (suggested: ${e.suggested_action.toLowerCase()})`, sev: e.severity }))\n];\nconst issuesHtml = issueRows.length\n  ? `<table width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;margin-top:6px\"><tr><th style=\"${th}\">Area</th><th style=\"${th}\">What we found</th><th style=\"${th}\">Level</th></tr>` +\n    issueRows.map(r => `<tr><td style=\"${td}\">${esc(r.area)}<br><strong>${esc(r.name)}</strong></td><td style=\"${td}\">${esc(r.detail)}</td><td style=\"${td}\">${chip(r.sev, sevColor[r.sev])}</td></tr>`).join('') + '</table>'\n  : '<p style=\"margin:6px 0;color:#16a34a\">No issues found. Everything looks good.</p>';\n\nconst readingsHtml = arr(ctx.readings_table).length\n  ? `<h3 style=\"margin:22px 0 4px;font-size:15px\">Today's readings</h3><table width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><th style=\"${th}\">Test</th><th style=\"${th}\">Result</th><th style=\"${th}\">Target</th><th style=\"${th}\">Status</th></tr>` +\n    ctx.readings_table.map(r => `<tr><td style=\"${td}\">${esc(r.label)}</td><td style=\"${td}\"><strong>${esc(r.value)}</strong></td><td style=\"${td}\">${esc(r.target)}</td><td style=\"${td}\">${chip(r.status, r.status === 'OK' ? '#16a34a' : '#dc2626')}</td></tr>`).join('') + '</table>'\n  : '';\n\nconst doneHtml = actions.length ? `<h3 style=\"margin:22px 0 4px;font-size:15px\">What we did today</h3><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 0 18px;padding:0;font-size:14px\">${actions.map(a => `<li>${esc(a)}</li>`).join('')}</ul>` : '';\nconst swimHtml = swim ? `<div style=\"background:#fef3c7;border-left:4px solid #d97706;padding:10px 14px;margin:18px 0;font-size:14px\"><strong>Note from your technician:</strong> ${esc(swim)}</div>` : '';\nconst nextHtml = `<div style=\"background:#f0f9ff;border:1px solid #bae6fd;border-radius:8px;padding:14px 16px;margin-top:22px;font-size:14px\">\n  <strong>${followUp ? 'Recommended follow-up: ' + esc(ftype) : 'No follow-up needed'}</strong><br>\n  Next visit: <strong>${esc(nextDate)}</strong> (in ${effDays} day${effDays === 1 ? '' : 's'})\n  ${quoteNeeded ? '<br><span style=\"color:#6b7280\">Our office will contact you about the recommended equipment work.</span>' : ''}\n</div>`;\n\nconst reportHtml = `<div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;max-width:620px;margin:auto;color:#1f2937\">\n  <div style=\"background:${C.BRAND};color:#fff;padding:18px 22px;border-radius:10px 10px 0 0\">\n    <div style=\"font-size:13px;opacity:.85\">${esc(C.COMPANY)}</div>\n    <h2 style=\"margin:2px 0 0;font-size:20px\">Pool Service Report</h2>\n    <div style=\"font-size:13px;opacity:.9;margin-top:4px\">${esc(visitDate)} &middot; ${esc(ctx.property_address)}</div>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"border:1px solid #e5e7eb;border-top:0;padding:22px;border-radius:0 0 10px 10px\">\n    <p style=\"margin-top:0\">Hello ${esc(ctx.customer_name)},</p>\n    <p style=\"font-size:15px\">${esc(ai.customer_summary)}</p>\n    <p style=\"margin:16px 0 8px\"><strong>Pool condition:</strong> ${chip(condition, condColor)} &nbsp; <strong>Water:</strong> ${esc(clarity)}</p>\n    ${swimHtml}\n    <h3 style=\"margin:22px 0 4px;font-size:15px\">Findings</h3>${issuesHtml}\n    ${readingsHtml}${doneHtml}${nextHtml}\n    <p style=\"font-size:12px;color:#6b7280;margin-top:22px\">Serviced by ${esc(ctx.technician)}. Questions? Reply to this email or call ${esc(C.PHONE)}.</p>\n  </div>\n</div>`;\n\n// ---------- 9. manager approval email ----------\nconst approvalHtml = `<div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;max-width:620px;margin:auto;color:#1f2937\">\n  <h2 style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">Report needs your approval</h2>\n  <p style=\"margin:0 0 12px;color:#6b7280\">${esc(ctx.customer_name)} &middot; ${esc(ctx.property_address)} &middot; ${esc(visitId)}</p>\n  <div style=\"background:#fef2f2;border-left:4px solid #dc2626;padding:10px 14px;margin-bottom:14px\"><strong>Why it was held</strong><ul style=\"margin:6px 0 0 18px;padding:0\">${reasons.map(r => `<li>${esc(r)}</li>`).join('')}</ul></div>\n  <p><strong>Technician (${esc(ctx.technician)}) wrote:</strong><br><em>${esc(ctx.raw_notes)}</em></p>\n  <p><strong>Structured as:</strong> ${esc(condition)} | Chem: ${esc(chemText)} | Equip: ${esc(equipText)}<br>\n     <strong>Follow-up:</strong> ${followUp ? esc(ftype) : 'No'} | <strong>Next visit:</strong> ${esc(nextDate)}</p>\n  <p><strong>Customer will see:</strong><br>${esc(ai.customer_summary)}</p>\n  <p style=\"margin-top:20px\">\n    <a href=\"__APPROVE__\" style=\"background:#16a34a;color:#fff;padding:10px 20px;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:bold\">Approve &amp; send</a>\n    &nbsp;\n    <a href=\"__REJECT__\" style=\"background:#6b7280;color:#fff;padding:10px 20px;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:bold\">Hold (don't send)</a>\n  </p>\n</div>`;\n\nconst opsAlert = `🚨 <b>URGENT pool visit</b>\\n<b>Customer:</b> ${esc(ctx.customer_name)} (${esc(ctx.customer_id)})\\n<b>Address:</b> ${esc(ctx.property_address)}\\n<b>Tech:</b> ${esc(ctx.technician)}\\n<b>Condition:</b> ${esc(condition)}\\n<b>Chem:</b> ${esc(chemText)}\\n<b>Equip:</b> ${esc(equipText)}\\n<b>Safety:</b> ${esc(safety.join('; ') || 'None')}\\n<b>Next visit:</b> ${esc(nextDate)}\\n<b>Visit:</b> ${esc(visitId)}`;\n\nreturn [{ json: {\n  visit_id: visitId, logged_at: $now.toISO(), visit_date: visitDate,\n  customer_id: ctx.customer_id, customer_name: ctx.customer_name, customer_email: ctx.customer_email,\n  property_address: ctx.property_address, technician: ctx.technician, raw_notes: ctx.raw_notes,\n  readings_text: ctx.readings_text, pool_condition: condition, water_clarity: clarity,\n  chemical_issues: chemText, equipment_issues: equipText, actions_taken: actions.join('; ') || 'None noted',\n  safety_concerns: safety.join('; ') || 'None',\n  rule_flags: arr(ctx.rule_flags).map(f => `${f.parameter || f.equipment}: ${f.issue}`).join('; ') || 'None',\n  recurring_flags: recurring.join('; ') || 'None',\n  follow_up_needed: followUp ? 'Yes' : 'No', follow_up_type: ftype, urgency, priority,\n  next_visit_days: effDays, next_visit_date: nextDate, confidence,\n  missing_info: missing.join('; '), needs_approval: needsApproval ? 'Yes' : 'No', work_order_id: woId,\n  customer_summary: String(ai.customer_summary || ''),\n  report_status: needsApproval ? 'Pending manager approval' : 'Sending', sent_at: '',\n  // helpers\n  open_issues: openIssues, quote_needed: quoteNeeded ? 'Yes' : 'No', wo_status: 'Open',\n  wo_assigned: ctx.assigned_tech || ctx.technician,\n  wo_description: `${ftype}: ${openIssues}` + (recurring.length ? ` | RECURRING: ${recurring.join('; ')}` : '') + (ai.internal_notes ? ` | Notes: ${ai.internal_notes}` : ''),\n  email_subject: `Your pool service report - ${visitDate} - ${condition}`,\n  report_html: reportHtml, approval_html: approvalHtml, ops_alert: opsAlert\n} }];"},"typeVersion":2},{"id":"c95fe72a-5d99-4520-ad98-8bbadae184c5","name":"Append Visit to Sheets","type":"n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets","position":[6400,1680],"parameters":{"columns":{"value":{"Address":"={{ $json.property_address }}","Urgency":"={{ $json.urgency }}","Customer":"={{ $json.customer_name }}","Priority":"={{ $json.priority }}","Readings":"={{ $json.readings_text }}","Visit ID":"={{ $json.visit_id }}","Logged At":"={{ $json.logged_at }}","Raw Notes":"={{ $json.raw_notes }}","Rule Flags":"={{ $json.rule_flags }}","Technician":"={{ $json.technician }}","Visit Date":"={{ $json.visit_date }}","Customer ID":"={{ $json.customer_id }}","Missing Info":"={{ $json.missing_info }}","AI Confidence":"={{ $json.confidence }}","Actions Taken":"={{ $json.actions_taken }}","Report Status":"={{ $json.report_status }}","Water Clarity":"={{ $json.water_clarity }}","Work Order ID":"={{ $json.work_order_id }}","Customer Email":"={{ $json.customer_email }}","Follow-Up Type":"={{ $json.follow_up_type }}","Needs Approval":"={{ $json.needs_approval }}","Pool Condition":"={{ $json.pool_condition }}","Report Sent At":"={{ $json.sent_at }}","Chemical Issues":"={{ $json.chemical_issues }}","Next Visit Date":"={{ $json.next_visit_date }}","Next Visit Days":"={{ $json.next_visit_days }}","Safety Concerns":"={{ $json.safety_concerns }}","Customer Summary":"={{ $json.customer_summary }}","Equipment Issues":"={{ $json.equipment_issues }}","Follow-Up Needed":"={{ $json.follow_up_needed }}","Recurring Issues":"={{ $json.recurring_flags }}"},"schema":[{"id":"Visit ID","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Visit ID","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Logged At","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Logged At","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Visit Date","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Visit Date","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Customer ID","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Customer ID","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Customer","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Customer","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Customer Email","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Customer Email","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Address","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Address","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Technician","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Technician","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Raw Notes","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Raw Notes","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Readings","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Readings","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Pool Condition","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Pool Condition","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Water Clarity","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Water Clarity","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Chemical Issues","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Chemical Issues","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Equipment Issues","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Equipment Issues","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Actions Taken","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Actions Taken","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Safety Concerns","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Safety Concerns","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Rule Flags","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Rule Flags","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Recurring Issues","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Recurring Issues","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Follow-Up Needed","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Follow-Up Needed","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Follow-Up Type","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Follow-Up Type","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Urgency","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Urgency","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Priority","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Priority","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Next Visit Days","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Next Visit Days","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Next Visit Date","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Next Visit Date","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"AI Confidence","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"AI Confidence","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Missing Info","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Missing Info","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Needs Approval","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Needs Approval","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Work Order ID","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Work Order ID","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Customer Summary","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Customer Summary","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Report Status","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Report Status","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Report Sent At","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Report Sent At","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true}],"mappingMode":"defineBelow","matchingColumns":[]},"options":{"cellFormat":"RAW"},"operation":"append","sheetName":{"__rl":true,"mode":"name","value":"Visits"},"documentId":{"__rl":true,"mode":"id","value":"1dx-1KrMuwi8POXiKNTix8induDZPPcycrBCchfx4kDM"},"authentication":"serviceAccount"},"credentials":{"googleApi":{"id":"credential-id","name":"Google Service Account account"}},"typeVersion":4.5},{"id":"6aaaef37-e8ca-423d-bca3-53236c304e55","name":"If Follow-Up Needed","type":"n8n-nodes-base.if","position":[6624,1680],"parameters":{"options":{},"conditions":{"options":{"version":2,"leftValue":"","caseSensitive":true,"typeValidation":"loose"},"combinator":"and","conditions":[{"id":"cf796a26-2a51-44db-8b12-500ce4291099","operator":{"type":"string","operation":"equals"},"leftValue":"={{ $('Build Visit Record').first().json.follow_up_needed }}","rightValue":"Yes"}]}},"typeVersion":2.2},{"id":"389fda55-48e2-47c4-bcab-beb0e432d33e","name":"Append Work Order to Sheets","type":"n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets","position":[6848,1600],"parameters":{"columns":{"value":{"Status":"={{ $('Build Visit Record').first().json.wo_status }}","Address":"={{ $('Build Visit Record').first().json.property_address }}","Customer":"={{ $('Build Visit Record').first().json.customer_name }}","Due Date":"={{ $('Build Visit Record').first().json.next_visit_date }}","Priority":"={{ $('Build Visit Record').first().json.priority }}","Visit ID":"={{ $('Build Visit Record').first().json.visit_id }}","Task Type":"={{ $('Build Visit Record').first().json.follow_up_type }}","Created At":"={{ $('Build Visit Record').first().json.logged_at }}","Customer ID":"={{ $('Build Visit Record').first().json.customer_id }}","Description":"={{ $('Build Visit Record').first().json.wo_description }}","Quote Needed":"={{ $('Build Visit Record').first().json.quote_needed }}","Assigned Tech":"={{ $('Build Visit Record').first().json.wo_assigned }}","Work Order ID":"={{ $('Build Visit Record').first().json.work_order_id }}"},"schema":[{"id":"Work Order ID","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Work Order ID","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Created At","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Created At","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Visit ID","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Visit ID","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Customer ID","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Customer ID","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Customer","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Customer","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Address","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"Address","defaultMatch":fal